API reference
=============

Base URL is /api. Every path below is relative to it.

Auth column:
	-       public
	user    valid access token required
	admin   valid access token with role admin

Success bodies are { success: true, ... }. Errors come from
middleware/errorHandler.ts as { success: false, message, errors? } with an
appropriate status. A 401 on a user route means the access token is missing or
expired; both clients respond by calling /auth/refresh once and retrying.


Auth  /auth
-----------

	POST   /auth/register              -      register a student, sends OTP
	POST   /auth/login                 -      returns access + refresh tokens
	POST   /auth/verify-email          -      consume the email OTP
	POST   /auth/resend-verification   -      reissue the email OTP
	POST   /auth/forgot-password       -      send a reset OTP
	POST   /auth/verify-reset-code     -      check the reset OTP
	POST   /auth/reset-password        -      set a new password
	POST   /auth/refresh               -      exchange refresh for access
	POST   /auth/logout                -      revoke the refresh token

All request bodies are validated by zod schemas in
src/validators/authValidator.ts before the controller runs. A validation
failure returns 400 with an errors array.


Admin  /admin
-------------

	POST   /admin/login                -      staff login
	GET    /admin                      admin  list admin accounts
	POST   /admin                      admin  create an admin account
	DELETE /admin/:id                  admin  remove an admin account


User  /user
-----------

	GET    /user/me                    user   live profile
	GET    /user/all                   admin  all students

/user/me is the mobile home screen's source of truth. It returns totalXp,
level, xpIntoLevel, xpMax, xpToNext, streak, loggedToday and totalWorkouts.
Level and streak are computed on the fly, never read from user_stats.


Challenges  /challenge
----------------------

	GET    /challenge/me               user   challenges this user joined
	GET    /challenge/active           -      active challenges
	GET    /challenge/all              -      every challenge
	GET    /challenge/pending          admin  challenges awaiting review
	POST   /challenge/category         user   filter by category
	POST   /challenge/add              admin  create a challenge
	POST   /challenge/:id/register     user   join
	GET    /challenge/:id/leaderboard  user   standings for one challenge
	POST   /challenge/:id/submit-points user  submit a result for validation
	GET    /challenge/:id/participants admin  roster with statuses
	DELETE /challenge/:id              admin  delete
	GET    /challenge/:id              user   one challenge

Route order matters. The bare GET /challenge/:id is registered last so that
/me, /active, /all and /pending are not swallowed by the parameter.

/challenge/active additionally returns recentParticipants, the three most
recent joiners per challenge, so the mobile browse cards can show real
avatars. It is fetched with two batched queries, not per challenge; keep it
that way.

submit-points is re-submittable. A student whose result was approved or
rejected may submit again, which resets the row to pending. It is only
blocked while a submission is already awaiting review.


Validations  /participants
--------------------------

	GET    /participants/pending           admin  the validation queue
	PATCH  /participants/:id/approve       admin  approve, award points
	PATCH  /participants/:id/reject        admin  reject

Approval is the only path that turns a submitted result into leaderboard XP.


Quests  /quest
--------------

	GET    /quest/list                 user   the whole quest bank
	GET    /quest/daily                user   today's active quests
	PUT    /quest/set-daily            admin  pin quests to a date
	DELETE /quest/daily/:date          admin  clear a date's override
	POST   /quest/add                  admin  add to the bank
	DELETE /quest/:id                  admin  remove from the bank
	POST   /quest/:id/claim            user   claim a quest's XP

set-daily takes a date key and an array of quest ids. Clearing an override
returns that date to the deterministic selection.

/quest/:id/claim currently has no completion record and no idempotency guard.
Read docs/maintenance.md before building on it.


Activities  /activity
---------------------

	GET    /activity/badge-template    user   badge template for an activity
	POST   /activity/create            user   create an activity
	GET    /activity/all               user   the activity catalogue
	POST   /activity/:id/award-points  user   log against an activity


Areas  /area
------------

	GET    /area                       user   areas with sub-activities
	POST   /area                       admin  add an area
	DELETE /area/:id                   admin  remove an area
	POST   /area/:id/activity          admin  add a sub-activity
	DELETE /area/:id/activity/:subId   admin  remove a sub-activity

Every mutation emits areas:updated so the mobile log screen refreshes its
catalogue without a restart.


Custom activities  /custom-activity
-----------------------------------

	GET    /custom-activity            user   this user's custom entries
	POST   /custom-activity            user   create one
	PATCH  /custom-activity/:id/pin    user   pin or unpin
	DELETE /custom-activity/:id        user   delete


Exercise  /exercise
-------------------

	POST   /exercise/log               user   log a session
	GET    /exercise/history           user   session history

Logging writes an ExerciseSession, increments users.totalXp and runs the
exercise badge evaluation, all inside one transaction.


Stats  /stats
-------------

	GET    /stats/exercises            user   distinct exercises logged
	GET    /stats/summary              user   headline totals
	GET    /stats/exercise/:key        user   per-exercise time series

/stats/exercise/:key backs the exercise detail screen and its range selector.


Leaderboards  /leaderboard
--------------------------

	GET    /leaderboard/faculty        user   grouped by faculty
	GET    /leaderboard/campus         user   individual campus-wide

Both include facultyKey and level per entry so a client can render the right
avatar tier and accent without a second lookup.


Check-in  /checkin
------------------

	POST   /checkin                    user   check in at the TLC
	GET    /checkin/status             user   whether today is done

A check-in is worth 75 XP and is stored as an ExerciseSession with
exerciseKey "gym-checkin". The endpoint is idempotent per day: a second call
returns alreadyCheckedIn without granting XP again.


Badges  /badge
--------------

	GET    /badge/all                  -      badge catalogue
	GET    /badge/me                   user   badges this user has earned
	POST   /badge/add                  admin  create a badge
	DELETE /badge/:badgeId             admin  delete a badge


Push  /push
-----------

	POST   /push/register              user   store an Expo push token
	DELETE /push/register              user   remove it on logout


Adding an endpoint
------------------

Register the route, wrap the controller in asyncHandler, return through a
serializer, emit a socket event if a client should react to it, and add a row
to this file in the same commit.